  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef loves bitwise operations. So, he creates the following problem but needs your help to solve it.\n\nChef calls a sequence of integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ `tasty` if it satisfies the following condition:\n\n\nparity(Ai&amp;Ai+1)≠parity(Ai∣Ai+1)parity(A_i \\&amp; A_{i+1}) \\neq parity(A_i | A_{i+1})parity(Ai​&amp;Ai+1​)=parity(Ai​∣Ai+1​) for 1≤i&lt;N1 \\leq i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N.\nChef gives you a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. You may perform the following operation on the sequence any number of times (possibly 000):\n\n\nChoose 222 indices iii and jjj (1≤i,j≤n1 \\le i, j \\le n1≤i,j≤n ; i≠ji \\neq ji=j) and change AiA_iAi​ to Ai⊕AjA_i \\oplus A_jAi​⊕Aj​.\nChef is asking you to make the sequence `tasty` using the **minimum** number of operations, or report that it is impossible.\n\nAs a friendly reminder,\n\n\nparity(x)parity(x)parity(x) denotes the remainder of dividing xxx by 222\n&amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes the bitwise AND operation\n∣|∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation\n⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case:\n\n\n\nIf it is impossible to convert the given sequence into a `tasty` sequence using the given operations, print a single line containing the integer −1-1−1.\nOtherwise, first, print a line containing a single integer MMM ― the **minimum** number of operations you have to perform.\nThen, print MMM lines describing these operations in the order in which you want to perform them. For each kkk (1≤k≤M1 \\leq k \\leq M1≤k≤M), the kkk-th of these lines should contain two space-separated integers iii and jjj (1≤i,j≤n1 \\le i, j \\le n1≤i,j≤n ; i≠ji \\neq ji=j) ― the indices on which the kkk-th operation is performed.\n\n**If there are multiple solutions, you may find any one of them.**",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1031 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^31≤T≤3⋅103",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230 for each valid iii",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (100 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
